  baked into a `static` calls-site (verified in tracing-0.1.44/src/macros.rs), so it
  must be const-evaluable and can't carry a runtime `&'static str` section. A
  separate `install_tracing_bridge()` (tracing_subscriber::Layer) forwards ordinary
  `tracing::{debug,info,warn,error}!` calls from anywhere else in the process into
  the same sink (target = section), which is what "on tracing" buys future
  modules. `libc::localtime_r`/`libc::atexit` used for exact parity with the C++'s
  localtime_r/atexit flush registration (both behind SAFETY comments). One bug
  caught by the mandatory pre-done review (rule 3): the console write wasn't
  covered by the same lock as the file write (C++'s single `scoped_lock` spans
  both); fixed by widening the `FILE_STATE` mutex's scope over the whole
  `log_message` body. Tests: unit tests in log.rs for format-string parity
  (console/file prefix, ANSI codes, capping, UTF-8 boundary safety) +
  crates/noctalia-core/tests/log_test.rs, a direct port of tests/log_test.cpp
  (level parsing, env var filtering incl. case-sensitivity/invalid-value handling,
  capped-line file test, rotation test) as one sequential #[test] (matches the
