## 2026-07-28 (session 7)
Attempted: task 1.5 — event-loop skeleton.
Done: 1.5. `noctalia-core::event_loop` (crates/noctalia-core/src/event_loop.rs).
  No C++ source for this — the C++ has its own hand-rolled poll-based MainLoop
  instead; this is new infrastructure implementing architecture decision 1.
  `EventLoop<Data>` wraps a `calloop::EventLoop<'static, Data>` plus a
  `TokioSidecar`: one dedicated OS thread running a *current-thread* tokio
  runtime (not the multi-worker scheduler — a desktop shell shouldn't spin up
  extra OS threads by default), parked for its whole life in
  `runtime.block_on(shutdown_rx.await)`. `spawn_on_tokio(future, on_complete)`
  spawns `future` via `Handle::spawn` (callable from any thread, including the
  main one) and reuses task 1.4's `timing::DeferredCall<Data>` as the tokio-to-
  calloop bridge (send a boxed closure through DeferredCall's channel; it runs
  `on_complete` on the main loop thread next dispatch) — no new channel type
  needed, DeferredCall already is "any thread can post a closure that runs on
  the main loop." Made `timing::deferred::Job<Data>` `pub(crate)` (was private)
  so event_loop.rs can name the alias.
  Pre-done review (rule 3) verified the crux design claim against tokio
  1.53.1's actual scheduler source (not just the code comment): a task spawned
  cross-thread via Handle::spawn onto a current-thread runtime reliably wakes
  a thread parked in block_on via the injection-queue + unpark path
  (scheduler/current_thread/mod.rs's Schedule::schedule and Wake::wake_by_ref),
  independent of whether the parked future itself ever completes. Also traced
  the shutdown/error paths (oneshot Sender-dropped-vs-sent, Builder::build()
  failure inside the sidecar thread) for hang/leak risk — none found. One
  nitpick: the `macros` tokio feature was enabled but unused (no tokio::test/
  select!/etc. anywhere) — dropped, confirmed tokio-macros no longer appears in
  the dependency tree.
  Tests: round_trips_a_message_through_the_tokio_sidecar_and_back (a real
  tokio::time::sleep task, bounded polling via repeated dispatch(), the literal
  Done criterion), main_thread_can_defer_work_onto_itself (defer() wrapper),
  tokio_handle_can_be_used_to_spawn_from_outside_spawn_on_tokio (the raw
  tokio_handle() accessor path). Added tokio (rt, sync, time features only) as
  a dependency; checked cargo tree -i openssl-sys -> nothing depends on it.
